# Nemotron 3 Nano 30B-A3B on a node of 8 GPUs, as Megatron-Bridge's performance summary
# benchmarks it (26.06: 37,316 tokens a second a GPU on 8 B300s, MXFP8, EP=8, a global
# batch of 512 rows of 8192 in microbatches of 4 rows a GPU). Every matmul is in MXFP8,
# since Megatron's MXFP8 recipe keeps no layer in bfloat16. The experts are sorted
# under FSDP, or split over the GPUs by NCCL EP, and routed by random logits as
# Megatron's are.
#
#   python scripts/benchmark.py run examples/benchmarks/megatron_nano.bux --out new.json
use nemotron_3_nano_30b_a3b

experts.random_logits = true

mesh    = sorted:  mesh(fsdp=8)
        | nccl_ep: mesh(expert=8)
methods = sorted:  methods(moe=sorted, microbatches=16, gather=layer)
        | nccl_ep: methods(moe=nccl_ep, capacity=1.25, microbatches=16)

data      = synthetic
optimizer = adamw(lr=3e-4)
seq_len   = 8192
batch     = 512
steps     = 12
log       = log(every=3)
precision = precision(compute=bfloat16, matmuls=mxfp8)
